---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/docs/CodeBlock.astro'
import Callout from '../../../components/docs/Callout.astro'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Issuing Credentials"
  description="VCIssuer API reference for the Attestto VC SDK. Configuration, issue options, schema plugins, and full code examples."
  currentPath="/docs/credentials/issuing/"
>
  <h1>Issuing Credentials</h1>
  <p class="docs-hero-sub">
    Create W3C Verifiable Credentials with the <code>VCIssuer</code> class.
    Configure your DID, sign with Ed25519 or ES256, and extend with schema plugins.
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>

  <CodeBlock lang="Terminal">
<Fragment set:html={`npm install <span class="c-str">@attestto-com/vc-sdk</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>IssuerConfig</h2>
  <p>Pass an <code>IssuerConfig</code> object when constructing the issuer:</p>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="IssuerConfig interface">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">interface</span> <span class="c-typ">IssuerConfig</span> <span class="c-br">{</span>
  did: <span class="c-typ">string</span>              <span class="c-cm">// Issuer DID (e.g. 'did:web:example.com')</span>
  privateKey: <span class="c-typ">Uint8Array</span>   <span class="c-cm">// Private key bytes</span>
  algorithm<span class="c-op">?</span>: <span class="c-str">'Ed25519'</span> <span class="c-op">|</span> <span class="c-str">'ES256'</span>  <span class="c-cm">// Default: 'Ed25519'</span>
  keyId<span class="c-op">?</span>: <span class="c-typ">string</span>          <span class="c-cm">// Verification method ID (default: did + '#key-1')</span>
<span class="c-br">}</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="Basic issuer setup">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">import</span> <span class="c-br">{</span> VCIssuer, generateKeyPair <span class="c-br">}</span> <span class="c-kw">from</span> <span class="c-str">'@attestto-com/vc-sdk'</span>

<span class="c-kw">const</span> keys = <span class="c-fn">generateKeyPair</span>()

<span class="c-kw">const</span> issuer = <span class="c-kw">new</span> <span class="c-fn">VCIssuer</span>(<span class="c-br">{</span>
  did: <span class="c-str">'did:web:my-org.example.com'</span>,
  privateKey: keys.privateKey,
  algorithm: <span class="c-str">'Ed25519'</span>,
  keyId: <span class="c-str">'did:web:my-org.example.com#signing-key-2026'</span>,
<span class="c-br">}</span>)`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>IssueOptions</h2>
  <p>The <code>issue()</code> method accepts these options:</p>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="IssueOptions interface">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">interface</span> <span class="c-typ">IssueOptions</span> <span class="c-br">{</span>
  type: <span class="c-typ">string</span> <span class="c-op">|</span> <span class="c-typ">string</span>[]     <span class="c-cm">// Credential type(s) — added to ['VerifiableCredential']</span>
  subjectDid: <span class="c-typ">string</span>          <span class="c-cm">// The subject's DID</span>
  claims: <span class="c-typ">Record</span><span class="c-op">&lt;</span><span class="c-typ">string</span>, <span class="c-typ">unknown</span><span class="c-op">&gt;</span>  <span class="c-cm">// Claims about the subject</span>
  context<span class="c-op">?</span>: <span class="c-typ">string</span> <span class="c-op">|</span> <span class="c-typ">string</span>[] <span class="c-cm">// Additional JSON-LD @context URIs</span>
  expirationDate<span class="c-op">?</span>: <span class="c-typ">string</span>    <span class="c-cm">// ISO 8601 expiration timestamp</span>
  credentialStatus<span class="c-op">?</span>: <span class="c-br">{</span>      <span class="c-cm">// Optional revocation endpoint</span>
    id: <span class="c-typ">string</span>
    type: <span class="c-typ">string</span>
  <span class="c-br">}</span>
  id<span class="c-op">?</span>: <span class="c-typ">string</span>                 <span class="c-cm">// Credential ID (auto-generated UUID if omitted)</span>
<span class="c-br">}</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>Issuing a credential</h2>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="issue-credential.ts">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">const</span> vc = <span class="c-kw">await</span> issuer.<span class="c-fn">issue</span>(<span class="c-br">{</span>
  type: <span class="c-str">'ProfessionalLicense'</span>,
  subjectDid: <span class="c-str">'did:web:holder.example.com'</span>,
  claims: <span class="c-br">{</span>
    profession: <span class="c-str">'Civil Engineer'</span>,
    licenseNumber: <span class="c-str">'CE-2026-1234'</span>,
    jurisdiction: <span class="c-str">'Costa Rica'</span>,
  <span class="c-br">}</span>,
  expirationDate: <span class="c-str">'2028-12-31T23:59:59Z'</span>,
  credentialStatus: <span class="c-br">{</span>
    id: <span class="c-str">'https://status.example.com/credentials/1'</span>,
    type: <span class="c-str">'StatusList2021Entry'</span>,
  <span class="c-br">}</span>,
<span class="c-br">}</span>)

console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(vc.id)     <span class="c-cm">// 'urn:uuid:...' (auto-generated)</span>
console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(vc.type)   <span class="c-cm">// ['VerifiableCredential', 'ProfessionalLicense']</span>
console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(vc.proof)  <span class="c-cm">// { type: 'Ed25519Signature2020', ... }</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>Multiple types</h2>
  <p>Pass an array to <code>type</code> to apply multiple credential types:</p>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">const</span> vc = <span class="c-kw">await</span> issuer.<span class="c-fn">issue</span>(<span class="c-br">{</span>
  type: [<span class="c-str">'ProfessionalLicense'</span>, <span class="c-str">'GovernmentIssuedCredential'</span>],
  subjectDid: <span class="c-str">'did:web:holder.example.com'</span>,
  claims: <span class="c-br">{</span> profession: <span class="c-str">'Architect'</span> <span class="c-br">}</span>,
<span class="c-br">}</span>)
<span class="c-cm">// vc.type = ['VerifiableCredential', 'ProfessionalLicense', 'GovernmentIssuedCredential']</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>Schema plugins</h2>
  <p>
    Register schema plugins with <code>issuer.use()</code> to auto-inject JSON-LD contexts
    and validate claims against known types. Calls are chainable.
  </p>

  <CodeBlock lang="TypeScript" title="Using schema plugins">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">import</span> <span class="c-br">{</span> drivingLicenseSchema <span class="c-br">}</span> <span class="c-kw">from</span> <span class="c-str">'@attestto-com/cr-vc-schemas'</span>

issuer.<span class="c-fn">use</span>(drivingLicenseSchema)

<span class="c-cm">// Now issuing a 'DrivingLicense' type auto-injects the CR context</span>
<span class="c-kw">const</span> vc = <span class="c-kw">await</span> issuer.<span class="c-fn">issue</span>(<span class="c-br">{</span>
  type: <span class="c-str">'DrivingLicense'</span>,
  subjectDid: <span class="c-str">'did:web:holder.example.com'</span>,
  claims: <span class="c-br">{</span> licenseClass: <span class="c-str">'B1'</span>, fullName: <span class="c-str">'Jane Doe'</span> <span class="c-br">}</span>,
<span class="c-br">}</span>)`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <Callout type="info">
    <strong>Auto-generated IDs.</strong> When you omit the <code>id</code> option, the SDK
    generates a <code>urn:uuid:...</code> identifier automatically. Pass your own if you need
    deterministic credential IDs.
  </Callout>

